{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494540-is-there-anything-actually-about-the-weaver-or-wyrm-revealed-for-5th-yet","id":1494540,"title":"Is there anything actually about the Weaver or Wyrm revealed for 5th yet?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-07T11:39:42-07:00","id":1494540,"title":"Is there anything actually about the Weaver or Wyrm revealed for 5th yet?","content":"Was taking a look at a number of things about W5; with the new Retaliation book coming out sometime in the future and more details about the tribe changes being released, I'm curious as to what other alterations will be brought to light. However, there's one point that I feel like a lot of people are overlooking in W5; namely, have the Weaver and Wyrm actually been named specifically in any 5th Edition reveals yet? <br /> <br /> There's been some talk in some of the reveals about &quot;the forces of chaos and entropy&quot;, obviously; however, any antagonism that has been revealed is entirely on stuff like corporations and logging companies. There's been no actual specific mentions of the Wyrm or Weaver in any of the recent W5 stuff that's been revealed; all the antagonism seems to lie with either mundane threats or spirits, with no mention of either of the Triat members in sight. I'm not sure if we can count information released in Heart of the Forest or Crimson Thaw, if there was any information released in the first place; I'm pretty sure I remember reading that some major plot details have changed since then so those games might not be accurate anymore.<br /> <br /> Basically, everyone just seems to be assuming that the Wyrm or Weaver are there, as opposed to actually confirming it. Like with the Get of Fenris; everyone states that the Gets have &quot;fallen to the Wyrm&quot;, but didn't Achilli confirm on Twitter a while back that the Gets were &quot;merely&quot; in a state of nonstop Rage? No mention of Wyrm influence, from what I can tell.<br /> <br /> Has there been any official confirmed information, from Paradox, Achilli, or someone else, about the Wyrm or Weaver in W5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27528-just-some-guy","name":"Just Some Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T16:28:20-07:00","id":1494560,"title":"","content":"In general, there has been very very little specific stuff shown so far. Even the stuff we discuss is based mostly on hints, but the general state of the cosmology has not been mentioned at all. Note that all the descriptions so far have not used the words Wyrm or Weaver.<br /> <br /> As for the Get, they fell to the &quot;Haglust&quot; which is some strange new state that seems to drive them to extremes and as an opponent to the other Garou (see last year's brand update for that detail). Falling to the Wyrm was never mentioned, well except in Apocalypse, the book.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T07:56:32-07:00","id":1494601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494540-is-there-anything-actually-about-the-weaver-or-wyrm-revealed-for-5th-yet?p=1494560#post1494560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, there has been very very little specific stuff shown so far. Even the stuff we discuss is based mostly on hints, but the general state of the cosmology has not been mentioned at all. Note that all the descriptions so far have not used the words Wyrm or Weaver.<br /> <br /> As for the Get, they fell to the &quot;Haglust&quot; which is some strange new state that seems to drive them to extremes and as an opponent to the other Garou (see last year's brand update for that detail). Falling to the Wyrm was never mentioned, well except in Apocalypse, the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>And everyone in Apocalypse had some kind of scenario like that written out, so it's not like the Get were unique in that regard.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T14:42:50-07:00","id":1494622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> O